From cd19bacd4959781964530fd5ed54dcc17e576002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haritha Yellampalle <hyellamp@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 14:22:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] QCLINUX: thermal: qcom: Fix recursive locking issue during
 trip update

For platforms with higher thermal junction temperature specifications,
the thermal trip update path may hit a recursive locking scenario when
updating trips per thermal zone.

Avoid this by invoking tsens_thermal_zone_trip_update() without taking
the thermal zone lock, since the function is already expected to operate
without requiring the caller to hold it.

Change-Id: I8496cd449ac4eae7a9a33059a8dcf04d7bbad0d8
Signed-off-by: Gaurav Kohli <gaurav.kohli@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
index 7314e10c9956..46aa2131e1b7 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
@@ -1317,7 +1317,7 @@ static int tsens_nvmem_trip_update(struct thermal_zone_device *tz)
 	num_trips = thermal_zone_get_num_trips(tz);
 	/* First trip is for userspace, update all other trips. */
 	for (i = 1; i < num_trips; i++)
-		thermal_zone_device_exec(tz, tsens_thermal_zone_trip_update, i);
+		tsens_thermal_zone_trip_update(tz, i);
 
 	return 0;
 }
